Images and videos in docs/images/ and docs/media/ are captures of the Skywarden console.
The camera frames and maps shown in them come only from:

- the author's own recording (indoor corridor),
- synthetic scenes generated by this repository's code, and
- the TUM RGB-D Dataset, sequence fr3/walking_xyz, CC BY 4.0, Sturm et al., "A Benchmark
  for the Evaluation of RGB-D SLAM Systems", IROS 2012. Faces are pixelated; no person
  is identified or re-identified.

Some measurements reported in the documentation were made on videos published on
YouTube under the Creative Commons Attribution licence. They were used only as local
test inputs under that licence; their authors were not individually asked for
permission. For that reason no file, frame, screenshot or map derived from those videos
is included in this repository; only their titles, authors, links and the measured
numbers are cited. Authors who want a citation removed can open an issue.

Videos, datasets and model weights are not stored in this repository. They are
downloaded by the user from the links in the scripts and source records, under their
own licences (for example YOLOX weights, Apache-2.0). Some optional model weights used
only for local research comparisons are non-commercial (CC BY-NC 4.0) and are neither
included nor required.

Dependencies installed from requirements.txt (OpenCV, pycolmap/COLMAP, NumPy, SciPy and
others) are distributed under their own licences.
